{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/07lqzm","slideIndex":3,"text":"The scientific page accepts latitude, longitude, altitude, UTC start and duration up to 168 hours. It asks Horizons for observer ephemerides of the Sun and Earth.\nThe app samples at one-hour steps and reports azimuth/elevation and intervals where elevation is above zero. These are geometric estimates; local terrain shadowing and panel performance are not modeled. The separate lander game is pedagogical.\nSource: JPL Horizons API documentation https://ssd-api.jpl.nasa.gov/doc/horizons.html ; implementation https://github.com/ingewilly2018-cyber/jarsig-orbital"}
