{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/lzdcg9","slideIndex":4,"text":"Close by asking for feedback, not for endorsement: which coordinate conventions and data layers should be validated first, and what reference cases would make a useful evaluation set?\nNASA's 2024 Artemis III communication described nine candidate regions near the lunar South Pole and said those regions would continue to be investigated. Do not characterize this prototype as part of NASA's site-selection process.\nSources: NASA South Pole visualizations https://www.nasa.gov/gallery/lunar-south-pole-visualizations/ ; Artemis III candidate-region update https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/nasa-provides-update-on-artemis-iii-moon-landing-regions/ ; NASA NTRS https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20250011660 ; JARSIG source https://github.com/ingewilly2018-cyber/jarsig-orbital"}